<title>FRANCE: French shares extend losses on futures selling.</title>
<headline>French shares extend losses on futures selling.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French shares widened their losses in the afternoon due to sell orders from the futures market as stops were hit. Wall Street was also down. Paris broke the 3,000 level at the opening and set fresh records today.</p>
<p>* CAC-40 index down 24.85, or 0.83 percent,</p>
<p>at 2,963.16 at 1409 GMT</p>
<p>* CAC-40 July futures 2,972 vs 2,999 at</p>
<p>Wednesdays close.</p>
<p>* Broader SBF120 index down 15.92 at 2,023.44</p>
<p>* Volume was about 8.5 billion</p>
</text>
